Z||000008||dogtired||12-25-1999||03:27 AM||||Well OK!<BR>I have to respect RACER1's position!<BR>Often we are branded, demiscriminated against just because of what we drive. How many of you have gotten the evil eye of the local law enforcement agency, just because of what we drive? I my  friends go by the name dogtired, so what would that have to do with the way I drive?  Granted I am an old fart and most challanges when driving I igore. Ocasionally Ill drop the hammer, just to prove I still have what I built?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Haven't lost yet, but choose my battles.<BR>Dont take me wrong folks, I am a true believer in "to each their own".<BR>Lets just keep out machines on the road and have fun in our own ways.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I may have tore a hole in the seat of my flame suit, but I have it on!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 12-25-1999).]||||reg||6
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-26-1999||06:48 PM||||Hello, dog, you old fart!  Some of us get the evil eye from the local law enforcement agents just because we are we (um..because I am I...no, because me is I...no, that's not it either.  What I mean is:  because me am him...aw, forget it!)||||reg||1
Z||000010||RFMike||12-26-1999||10:40 PM||||You could do what I do when I'm not in the mood to be bugged about racing, which is most of the time.  Seen too much gristle on the road to be interested in being a grease spot.  Last week, on my way home on the freeway, a Plymouth Neon pulled alongside, speeded up, slowed, matched.  I looked over, and then laughed.  I made sure the guy could see me, and kept on laughing and slapping the steering wheel.  The look on his face was priceless.  He drove off, leaving me alone.  Now, in this case the laugh was appropriate, and I really wasn't faking it, but it has worked for me many times.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-27-1999||12:46 AM||||If you really want the racer in the next lane to leave you alone, wait til you get up to about 30mph, look him dead in the eye, and mash on your gas just long enough to chirp the tires.  He'll think, "If he can do that, I'd better not race him."  Or just do what I do.  Look him dead in the eye, give him a big wink, and pick your nose.  Either way he'll stop trying to race.||||reg||1
Z||000012||TOM||12-27-1999||12:03 PM||||Or blow him kisses. But he might want a date then.||||reg||1
Z||000013||bHooper||12-27-1999||12:38 PM||||Rf, I've done the laughing thing before. and it works wonders to p!$$ someone off!  Usually I'll do it to the kids in the wannabe's, you kow the civic's with the rollerskate offsets, or the muffler?  I love the reaction, and now that my Gt is on jack stands, I still find myself doing it from my Jeep  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
